  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1002 PM CDT Tue Jun 23 2026\n\nWe will enter into a more zonal pattern as we finish out the week.\nWeak disturbances will periodically ripple through this flow, \nkeeping low to medium rain and storm chances in the forecast \nthrough Saturday. These passages will move north of Middle TN, \nkeeping the better rain chances there, but areas along and north \nof I-40 will have a 30-50% chance for rain and storms through the\nweekend. \n\nThe heat will be the main storm as we head into next week. Temperatures\nwill continue to gradually rise each day this week as an \nexpansive area of high pressure treks toward the southeast. \nTemperatures will push into the 90s this weekend with mid 90s \nforecast Sunday. By Monday, highs will reach in to the mid to \nupper 90s, and this heat doesn't look to go anywhere fast. Upper \n90s are in the forecast through at least the first half of next \nweek. Heat index values during this time will reach into the 100s,\nso please keep this in mind if you have any outdoor interests \nthis weekend and early next week.",
